@@@!atrep-exo
@=at-org=>org

@@/ Org export for the at-org syntax mapper. Org has no escape
@@/ mechanism, so the escape table is empty; the canonical
@@/ subset is a fixed point of export then import. Example
@@/ blocks canonicalize to #+BEGIN_SRC.

@-> *document
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> *paragraph
@(grammata)

>-@

@-> *solo #
* @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *solo ##
** @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *solo ###
*** @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *solo ####
**** @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *solo #####
***** @(grammata)
>-@

@-> /
/@(grammata)/
>-@

@-> *
*@(grammata)*
>-@

@-> _
_@(grammata)_
>-@

@-> +
+@(grammata)+
>-@

@-> ><
[[@(grammata)]]
>-@

@-> >
#+BEGIN_QUOTE
@(grammata)
#+END_QUOTE
>-@

@-> ~
#+BEGIN_VERSE
@(grammata)
#+END_VERSE
>-@

@-> |
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> *strophe
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> *stichos
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> -
- @(grammata)
>-@

@-> .
@(taxis). @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ::
- @(lemma) :: @(grammata)
>-@

@-> ^
[fn:@(onym)] @(grammata)
>-@

@-> *deixis ^
[fn:@(onym)]
>-@

@-> *verbatim
#+BEGIN_SRC@[ @(genoses)]@
@(content)
#+END_SRC
>-@

@-> *verbatim-inline
~@(content)~
>-@

@-> *media
[[file:@((param))]]
>-@

@-> *onym-anchor
<<@(onym)>>
>-@
